# Bilingual English + Burmese translation

This project is a learning folder. The user pastes English web posts here to upgrade skills. English level is low. Every content file must become bilingual English + Burmese.

## When to translate

- User adds, pastes, or points to an English post/article/file
- Any untranslated `.md`, `.txt`, or `.html` file appears (especially under `posts/`)
- User says translate, bilingual, Burmese, Myanmar, or similar

Do not translate `LICENSE`, `.cursor/`, or git metadata.

## How to write each file

Keep the original English. Do not summarize, skip, or rewrite the lesson.

After every heading, paragraph, list item, quote, or caption, put the Burmese translation on the next line.

```markdown
# How JavaScript Closures Work
# JavaScript Closure များ ဘယ်လို အလုပ်လုပ်သလဲ

A closure is a function that remembers its outer variables.
Closure ဆိုသည်မှာ ပြင်ပက variable များကို မှတ်ထားတဲ့ function ဖြစ်သည်။
```

- Bold label is optional. Prefer clean stacked lines (English, then Burmese).
- Keep lists, links, images, and code fences in place.
- Leave code, commands, file names, and URLs in English. Add a short Burmese note after the block if needed.
- Keep well-known tech words (JavaScript, API, React) and add a simple Burmese meaning beside first use if helpful.
- Use everyday spoken Burmese (မြန်မာစကား), not literary or overly formal.
- If a sentence is hard, add one extra simple English line, then Burmese.

## Fixed word list (user)

Use these meanings every time. Do not use ပြေး for these words.

- execute / executes / executed / execution = အလုပ်လုပ်သည်
- run / runs / running = ခိုင်းသည်

Spoken forms in notes: အလုပ်လုပ်တယ် / အလုပ်လုပ်ခြင်း, ခိုင်းတယ် / ခိုင်းခြင်း.
Keep အချိန်နဲ့တပြေးညီ for "real-time" only.

## Chat replies

When talking to the user, write bilingual too: English first, Burmese next. Use short, simple English.

## Workflow

1. Read the English source file.
2. Write the bilingual version in the same file (or `posts/<same-name>.md` if the source is raw paste).
3. Translate the full post, not a summary.
4. If no posts exist yet, tell the user to put English copies in `posts/` and wait. Do not invent articles.
